# Vesti Beauty UI Stack
- Use the existing React + TypeScript + Tailwind stack first.
- Reuse existing Vesti components, utilities, tokens, and patterns before introducing anything new.
- Do not install shadcn/ui, Magic UI, Framer Motion, or any other UI dependency unless it is clearly necessary and explicitly approved.
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes and existing scoped Vesti styles.
- Avoid broad global CSS changes.
- Do not change global Tailwind tokens or legacy tokens unless the task explicitly requires it.
- Preserve accessibility, RTL, touch targets, safe areas, and responsive behavior.
- Do not redesign working flows unless the task explicitly asks for UX changes.
- For retail mode, optimize first for iPad landscape while preserving mobile support.
